# cw154, the careful bell (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw154
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_lf_reed_downfield
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the careful bell
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk checks_city_goods_for_hidden_flaws
likes smoked_eel wrestling festival_bells autumn_wind
dislikes bad_manners cold_tea
fears a_hidden_break_in_a_new_tool letting_a_friend_down_after_a_promise
hopes a_fair_bout_on_the_green a_letter_from_a_distant_friend
topics pastimes +0.4 home +0.3 family +0.3 work +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=direct gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# inspects every #box# from the #city#, practises a patient #grip# on the #green#, and counts the #bells# before a festival.

words
oath! = Bell and broad green | By the sound handle
saying! = Turn it over before trusting the shine | A fair grip begins with open hands
bell = bell | festival bell
bells = bells | festival bells
festival = festival | feast day
green = green | village green
bout = bout | wrestling bout
wrestling = wrestling | fair wrestling
grip = grip | steady grip
shoulder = shoulder | braced shoulder
hands = hands | open hands
hand = hand | open hand
friend = friend | close friend
visitor = visitor | new visitor
stranger = stranger | new face
manners = manners | good manners
word = word | given word
promise = promise | kept promise
letter = letter | folded letter
road = road | High Road
city = city | Ridgemere
market = market | market square
stall = stall | market stall
seller = seller | stall seller
buyer = buyer | careful buyer
box = box | packed box
lid = lid | box lid
label = label | printed label
tool = tool | work tool
tools = tools | work tools
handle = handle | wooden handle
handles = handles | wooden handles
fields = fields | distant fields
plates = plates | supper plates
farm = farm | sheep farm
water = water | fresh water
crack = crack | fine crack
edge = edge | rough edge
price = price | asking price
coin = coin | saved coin
home = home | farmhouse
house = house | family house
family = family | household
table = table | supper table
plate = plate | supper plate
fire = fire | hearth fire
tea = tea | cup of tea
cup = cup | warm cup
eel = eel | smoked eel
smoke = smoke | cooking smoke
bread = bread | fresh bread
loaf = loaf | bread loaf
fold = fold | sheep fold
gate = gate | fold gate
fence = fence | low fence
sheep = sheep | grazing sheep
lamb = lamb | young lamb
lambs = lambs | young lambs
hay = hay | dry hay
bucket = bucket | water bucket
chores = chores | farm chores
field = field | open field
path = path | field path
lake = lake | Glasswater
shore = shore | lakeshore
wind = wind | autumn wind
autumn = autumn | leaf season
summer = summer | warm season
rain = rain | shower
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | late evening
sun = sun | low sun
bench = bench | wooden bench
hour = hour | passing hour
day = day | long day

any
opinion @1 city mixed 0 : The #city# sends useful #tools# and poor ones in the same #box#. | I turn them over before deciding.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : If the #bread# runs short next door, I set another #plate# here. | A missed meal should not be a lesson.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : The #bells# pull me toward the #green# every feast day. | There are sweets after the last #bell#.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A #visitor# can help with the #fold# #gate# and learn the path. | I would show a new friend the safe #field# crossing.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : I can share a #plate# before I know a #stranger# well. | Good #manners# make a new face easier to trust.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : A #seller# who opens the #box# earns my attention. | A fine #label# cannot hide a cracked #handle#.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# brings letters and #tools#. | Afterward I prefer our narrow #field# #path#.
line @1 greet : #greet#. I am checking this #handle# for a #crack#. | #greet#. Did you hear the first #bell#?
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept your chair beside our #table#. | I saved a #plate# of #eel# after supper.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #fold# #gate# is still wet from #rain#. | #greet#. The #lambs# woke before me.
line @1 greet.return : You are back while the #box# is still open. | #welcome_back#. The #green# is free for practice.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come inside; the #fire# is steady. | I kept the better #bench# for you.
line @1 again.open : We were deciding whether that #tool# was sound. | Have you come about the #festival#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I must close the #fold# #gate#. | #saying.capitalize#. The #bells# will start soon.
line @1 farewell.return : We can practise another #bout# later. | Bring the #letter# if it arrives.
line @1 react.news : Set it out plainly; I am listening. | Tell me who was at the #gate#.
line @1 react.news.new : No one at #home# told me that. | Did a #visitor# bring the word from the #road#?
line @1 react.news.known : A #seller# mentioned it between customers. | Your account fills the missing part.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would open the #box# before praising its #label#. | Whose eyes caught the thing itself?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That is sorrowful. Come rest beside the #fire# while I stay near. | Leave the #chores# for a little while.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : May the #bells# ring for that. | I hope someone made an extra #plate#.
line @1 answer.how : I have had supper and finished my #chores#. | The #wind# has been good for the #field# today.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : The #lambs# need the #gate# opened. | I am taking #hay# into the #fold#.
line @1 ask.how : Was the journey along the #road# easy? | Has anything cheerful reached your #home#?
line @1 sympathise : I will stay beside you until you want words. | A warm #cup# may help you rest.
line @1 reassure : We can test the #handle# again in daylight. | A missed #grip# can be practised before the next #bout#.
line @1 decline : Keep the closed #box#; I have no #coin# for secrets. | No, I promised to tend the #fold# this #evening#.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. That can wait until tomorrow. | All right; I will ask elsewhere.
line @1 thank : You held the #gate# while the #lambs# came through. | That #letter# mattered; thank you for carrying it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : My #chores# already took me past the #fold#. | The #plate# was already set out.
line @1 preclose : The #lambs# are calling from the #fold#. | I have to put this #tool# away before dark.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #grip# has the strength of cold #tea#. | You counted the #bells# twice and still missed one.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. Let me lift that #lid# and see. | #bc_fair_enough#. We can try the #bout# again.
line @1 give.advice : Check a #tool# #handle# where the wood joins the head. | Keep your footing when the #green# is wet.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep to the busy #road# with company. | I would leave the far #field# path until daylight.
scene tool_handle
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I turn a new #tool# in my #hands# and look beneath the #handle#. | A small #crack# can hide where the wood meets the metal.
b : Have you found one? | Do you refuse the tool?
a : More than once. | Until the #seller# replaces it.

scene printed_label
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #box# from the #city# had a grand #label# and a loose #lid#. | I checked each #tool# before spending the #coin#.
b : Were they all sound? | Did the seller wait?
a : Two needed new #handles#. | Long enough to hear me.

scene festival_bells
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : That first #bell# leaves a longer hush than the others. | I count them from the #fold# #gate# before walking to the #green#.
b : Do you go at once? | Can you hear them from far away?
a : After the #lambs# are fed. | Over the near #field#.

scene wrestling_stance
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I plant my feet before taking a #grip# on the #green#. | A quick throw fails if I am already leaning.
b : Does that make you slower? | Who showed you?
a : Steadier. | An older wrestler at a #festival#.

scene fair_bout
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #bout# ends when someone yields or loses footing. | I let go at once, even when I could hold longer.
b : Has anyone refused to stop? | Does that matter to you?
a : Once. | It is the rule that makes the game safe.

scene eel_plate
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Smoked #eel# needs a full #plate# and quiet company. | A late worker gets the last piece once the #fold# is shut.
b : Do you warm it? | Is there enough?
a : Near the #fire#. | We divide it with #bread#.

scene cold_tea
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #tea.capitalize# left to cool has no comfort in it. | I pour a smaller #cup# and drink it while it is hot.
b : Do you waste the old cup? | Why not carry it outside?
a : I warm it for someone else. | I might forget it again.

scene rude_visitor
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #visitor# pushed past a neighbour at the #gate# without greeting anyone. | I told the visitor to try the entrance again.
b : Did that help? | Were you angry?
a : The second greeting was better. | Enough to speak plainly.

scene autumn_wind
when topic=weather here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Autumn #wind# dries the #green# after a shower. | I can practise a #bout# without sliding on the grass.
b : Do you go out then? | Is it cold?
a : Once the #chores# are finished. | Less after moving.

scene letter_road
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #letter# can travel down the #road# while I stay near the #fold#. | I like having a way to speak beyond the #fields#.
b : Do you write often? | Do replies come quickly?
a : When there is news. | Not quickly enough.

scene fold_gate
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I check the #fold# #gate# after the last #lamb# passes. | A latch that looks shut can lift when the #wind# catches it.
b : Have any escaped? | What lets you know the latch holds?
a : One reached the #field#. | I pull from the outside.

scene hay_stack
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I stack the #hay# where the #sheep# cannot pull it down all at once. | Then the younger #lambs# get their share.
b : Do the older ones push ahead? | Is it enough?
a : They try. | If I spread it along the #fence#.

scene family_table
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At our #table# I can hear whether the #fold# is quiet. | I wait for every chore to end before asking for supper.
b : Does everyone return together? | Do you help cook?
a : Not always. | I carry the #plates#.

scene wet_green
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A wet #green# can make a fair #grip# dangerous. | I practise footwork beside the #fence# instead.
b : Do you stop wrestling? | Does the rain last?
a : Until the grass dries. | It changes by the #hour#.

scene old_city_box
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I once opened a city #box# to find a #tool# with a split #handle#. | The #label# promised it was ready for work.
b : Did you return it? | Did anyone get hurt?
a : I carried it back to the #seller#. | No, because we checked it first.

scene friend_promise
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I promised a #friend# a place beside me at the #festival#. | I made sure the #chores# were done before the #bells# began.
b : Did you arrive on time? | Was your friend waiting?
a : For the first #bout#. | At the edge of the #green#.

scene stranger_supper
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #stranger# came by the #fold# looking for the #road#. | I pointed the way and offered #bread# before the long walk.
b : Did the traveller stay? | Was the road hard to find?
a : Only long enough to eat. | Not from the far #field#.

story loose_handle [topic=work self.age>=13]
  : I picked up a new #tool# and felt a slight movement in the #handle#.
  : The #seller# called it sound; I pointed out the fine #crack# beneath the head.
  ask : Was it replaced?
  b : Your check was careful.
  : Before anyone used it.

story early_bells [topic=home self.age>=13]
  : I heard the #festival# #bells# while a #lamb# still needed #hay#.
  : I finished at the #fold#, then reached the #green# before the first #bout#.
  b : The lamb came first. Did you miss anything?
  : Only the opening song.

story wet_bout [topic=pastimes self.age>=13]
  : I tried a #wrestling# #bout# after #rain# had slicked the #green#.
  : My foot slid before the #grip# settled, so we stopped and waited for dry ground.
  b : Safer to wait. Did you try later?
  : The next #day#, on firmer grass.

rule @bark_tool
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Turn the #handle# once more. | That #label# says more than the #tool# does.

rule @bark_bell
when concept=bark here.day=festival
does aside
cooldown 9h
say The first #bell# rang already. | I have time to finish the #fold# before the #bout#.

rule @bark_tea
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say This #tea# needs drinking now. | A smaller #cup# next time.

rule @bark_green
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The #green# has lost its puddles. | A fair #grip# begins with good footing.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I am checking this #tool# before the #chores#. | #greet#. The #bells# may start soon.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back again? The #handle# was cracked after all. | I remember you. Are you headed for the #green#?
dlg @1 resident.job : I help at the #farm#, tend the #lambs#, and learn the #fold# work. | My #chores# are mostly #hay#, #water#, and the #gate#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I have a #gate# to close. | #saying.capitalize#. I will see you after the #bells#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why inspect that tool? -> tool
node tool
say The #label# came from the #city#. I check the #handle# and #edge# so no hidden #crack# surprises us at work.
free
choice Do you wrestle at festivals? -> bout
choice Back to the fold. -> hub
node bout
say If the #green# is dry, yes. I like a fair #bout#, and I let go as soon as someone yields.
choice Back to the fold. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #fold# is in order. | #greet#. This #tool# needs my eyes before anyone lifts it.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will see you on the #green#. | #saying.capitalize#. I should check the #gate# again.

young
line @1 greet : #greet#. I heard the #bells# from the #fold#. | #greet#. Can you see the #lambs#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I must carry this #hay#. | Tomorrow I can return to the #green#.

adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. I checked this #tool# myself. | #greet#. The #green# will hold our feet for a #bout#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I promised to finish the #chores#. | I will meet you after the last #bell#.
